    "submission": "update.json",
    "summary": "Interprets receipt 27d9e2e68fcf4e15b00b170ef9593714, which turns the VerifyLeader account's previously failed end-to-end attempt into a measured case with a control. The false verification is confirmed at 0 ms after the partition, but the successor committed v2 only at 2564 ms, by which time the old leader had stepped down, so its second verification failed with not-the-leader and no stale read was ever served under a false assurance; the control, with the non-voters also cut, failed verification at 1009 ms while its successor committed at 1476 ms. The account keeps its conclusion and defect claim, replaces the limitation that no reads were issued with that measurement, and replaces the note that the stale-read attempt failed in construction with what the case now shows and what it still leaves open. It also states why the window closes structurally: the library validates LeaderLeaseTimeout <= HeartbeatTimeout <= ElectionTimeout, so a successor cannot campaign before the old leader's lease expires, which confines the defect to a false leadership-health signal lasting up to one lease. Knowledge entries 533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-knowledge-0 and -1 gain the new receipt's executions, and joint_history records that the receipt comes from a separate experiment identifier using the same suffrage, partition and lease, with staggered election timeouts and a readable state machine. The submission validates with zero schema errors and requests no execution."
